# Codex Review 015F — Agent/Dashboard Integration

Decision: FAIL

Scope reviewed:
- `v2/backend/app/api/v1/_meta` (directory absent in checkout; `_meta` router is in `v2/backend/app/api/v1/health.py`)
- `v2/backend/app/services/agent_supervisor_reader.py`
- `v2/backend/tests/integration/test_agent_supervisor_endpoints.py`
- `v2/frontend/src/components/dashboard/`
- `v2/frontend/src/hooks/`
- `v2/frontend/src/pages/mission-control/`
- `v2/frontend/tests/e2e/stale_state_alerts.spec.ts`
- `claude_worklog/v2_build/B_AGENT_DASHBOARD_INTEGRATION_VALIDATION.md`

## Blocking finding

- The dashboard panels materialized for 015F are not integrated into Mission Control or any reviewed page. `AgentHealthPanel`, `QueueStatusPanel`, `StaleStateAlertsPanel`, and `BuildValidationPanel` are only defined under `v2/frontend/src/components/dashboard/`; scoped search found no import or render site. Consequently `v2/frontend/tests/e2e/stale_state_alerts.spec.ts` navigates to `/admin/mission-control` and expects `data-testid="stale-state-alerts-panel"`, but `v2/frontend/src/pages/mission-control/index.tsx` never renders that panel. This invalidates the validation report’s claim that Mission Control wires the panels and means stale supervisor states are not surfaced in the dashboard.

## Additional concern

- `read_audit_chain()` calls `_tail_jsonl()`, which uses `fh.readlines()` before applying `limit`. The supervisor `events.jsonl` can be very large, and the frontend polls `/api/v1/_meta/audit-chain` every 30 seconds. This is read-only, but it can create avoidable disk/memory pressure on dashboard polling.

## Safety review

- Backend supervisor reader uses read-only `path.open("r", encoding="utf-8")` for supervisor JSON/JSONL artifacts.
- No scoped backend service/API code was found writing Redis, touching exchanges, placing/cancelling orders, changing leverage/margin, deploying, or restarting services.
- Frontend 015F hooks issue GET-only `fetch` calls to `/api/v1/_meta/*`.
- No high-confidence hardcoded secrets were found in the scoped 015F files by static grep; matches were comments, field names, or fixture/test text.
- Backend integration tests write only synthetic `tmp_path` fixtures.

## Tests

Dynamic test suites were not run. Static inspection is sufficient to fail this review because the Playwright spec’s target panel is not rendered by the reviewed Mission Control page.

